#!/usr/bin/env python3
r"""cc-arch — the architecture overview PDF follows the architecture, without anybody asking for it.

  cc-arch landed <repo|path>        what landed since last time; if one of those landings DECLARED itself an
                                    architecture revision, rebuild the overview and post it into #<repo>.
                                    Silence — no build, no message, no file — for everything else.
  cc-arch build <repo|path> [<ref>] rebuild from the living source at <ref> (default: the default branch as this
                                    checkout last saw it), verify it, print the path. Posts nothing.
  cc-arch marked <repo|path> <ref>  does the commit at <ref> declare an architecture revision? prints it, exit 0/1
  cc-arch selfcheck                 fixtures of its own: its own HOME, its own repos, a stub `cc-slack`

WHY IT EXISTS. The overview is the one document the owner reads to know what the box IS. Until this file, it was
rebuilt only when he asked, so the document and the system drifted apart between askings — and a stale picture of
a machine that runs itself is worse than none, because it is believed. The document now follows the code: the
source is in the repo beside the code it describes, and a landing that changes the shape of the box rebuilds it
and puts the PDF in the channel.

WHAT COUNTS IS DECLARED, NEVER INFERRED. Most landings are not architecture revisions, and a PDF after every
merge is noise that gets muted. So the change SAYS SO, in a commit message on its branch, on a line of its own
starting in the first column:

    ARCHITECTURE: <one line — what about the shape of the box is different now>

and nothing else here decides. No diff is read, no path is special, no model is asked. A PR that rewrites this
very source and says nothing posts nothing; that is the intended answer, not a gap.

WHY THE COMMIT MESSAGE AND NOT THE PR BODY. cc-land squash-merges, so every commit message on the branch is
carried into the squash commit on the default branch — and that commit is then IMMUTABLE and local. A PR body is
neither: it is fetched over the network, `gh pr edit` is not a gated command, and it can be rewritten AFTER the
merge, which would let whoever merged last choose the sentence this box says out loud in the owner's channel
(security review of #361). Reading it out of the landed commit closes that outright: what is posted is what was
reviewed, and this file needs no network at all. The declaration is still SANITIZED before it is said — see
`clean` — because "written by one of ours" is not the same as "safe to repeat verbatim".

WHERE IT IS CALLED FROM, AND WHY NOT FROM THE LANDING. cc-publish gives it a turn after it has pushed — that is
this box's one unattended "the shared code moved" moment, it already runs on a timer with nobody watching, and it
needs no unit of its own. It is deliberately NOT the landing: a landing is a long chain of steps that must not
grow a document build in the middle of it, and a merge that arrives some other way — the web, another machine —
must reach the channel just the same. Nothing here runs in a session's turn.
  The one thing that arrangement cannot see is a revision that changes NOTHING inside the published prefix: no
  publish, so no turn, so no document — it waits for the next landing that does touch it. That is a narrow miss
  and not a hidden one: the prefix is the generic system and the source of this document is inside it, so a shape
  change that misses it is one box's private overlay. `cc-arch landed <repo>` by hand covers that case.

THE CURSOR, AND WHY IT NEVER BACKFILLS. Each repo has one: the commit this file has already looked at. A first
run writes the current head and posts nothing at all, because the history behind it was landed by people who
never knew this file existed, and answering for it would mean a flood on the day it is installed. From then on
the range is exactly what landed since.

POST ONCE, KEYED ON THE COMMIT. The ledger records the landed SHA, not the PR number and not the cursor: a
cursor wound back re-reads the same commits and sends nothing, because those SHAs are already in it. The intent
is written down BEFORE the upload, so a process killed between the two leaves a record and the next turn does not
send the document a second time; an upload that comes back FAILED is written down as failed and is still owed, so
a channel that was down for a minute does not cost the owner the document. The ledger and the cursor are the two
things anybody wanting a second copy would delete, so cc-guard fences this directory against a gated session's
shell the way it fences ~/bin.

NOTHING IT WRITES FOLLOWS A SYMLINK. Every artifact, cursor and ledger line is opened O_NOFOLLOW (a new file
O_EXCL under a temp name, then renamed into place), because a planted link at any of those paths would otherwise
make this file write where somebody else chose (security review of #361).

AND IT IS VERIFIED BEFORE IT IS SENT. Plain pdflatex and the psnfss fonts, twice for the TikZ positions, with no
shell escape AND `openin_any=p openout_any=p`: the source arrives by a landing and is built, never trusted — a
`\input` of an absolute path would otherwise pull a file of this box's into a document that is about to be
uploaded, which no `-no-shell-escape` stops. Then `pdfinfo` for pages and `pdffonts` for embedding — a PDF whose
fonts are not in it renders as somebody else's guess on a phone. A build or a check that fails posts NOTHING and
leaves the cursor where it was, so the next turn tries again.
"""
import sys, os, re, json, time, shutil, subprocess, tempfile, fcntl

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
BIN = os.environ.get("CC_ARCH_BIN") or os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
STATE = f"{HOME}/.cc/state/arch"
# The declaration, in the first column of a line of its own: the squash commit keeps a branch commit's body lines
# exactly there, and requiring column 0 keeps the word inside a sentence — or an indented quotation of this very
# paragraph — from being read as somebody asking for a document.
MARK = re.compile(r"^ARCHITECTURE:[ \t]*(\S.*?)[ \t]*$", re.M)
# How a squash lands with its PR: GitHub appends `(#n)` to the subject, and cc-land squash-merges everything.
# Only ever used to SAY which PR it was; nothing is decided by it.
PRNUM = re.compile(r"\(#([0-9]{1,7})\)\s*$")
REC, FLD = "\x1e", "\x1f"      # separators for `git log --format`: a commit body carries newlines, tabs and pipes
# The living source, in the two shapes the tree has: the control repo carries the generic half under `core/`, the
# published repo IS that half. Overridable for a box whose overview lives somewhere else.
SRC_RELS = tuple(x for x in (os.environ.get("CC_ARCH_SOURCE"),) if x) or \
           ("core/docs/autobox-overview.tex", "docs/autobox-overview.tex")
REPO_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$")
GIT_TIMEOUT = 120
TEX_TIMEOUT = 90       # one pdflatex pass over a TikZ document; measured at ~1.5 s, so this is a hang's bound
POST_TIMEOUT = 180     # an upload, the same bound cc-land allows its own Slack calls
MSG_CAP = 300          # what one declaration may contribute to the message; the document says the rest
# TEX_TIMEOUT * 2 + POST_TIMEOUT is this file's worst case, and cc-publish's `timeout` around it is set from that.


class Stop(Exception):
    """Something outside this file could not answer. Nothing is posted and the cursor does not move."""


def sh(argv, cwd=None, timeout=GIT_TIMEOUT, env=None):
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(argv, cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout,
                           env=None if env is None else dict(os.environ, **env))
        return p.returncode, (p.stdout or "") + (p.stderr or "")
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        return 127, f"{e.__class__.__name__}: {e}"


def last(o, n=200):
    return " ".join((o or "").split())[-n:]


def write_new(path, data, mode=0o644):
    """Replace `path` without ever writing THROUGH it. A new file under a temp name — O_EXCL so a link planted at
    that name fails, O_NOFOLLOW so one planted at the path itself does — then renamed over the destination, which
    replaces a symlink rather than following it. ~/.cc/state is not a private directory by construction, so this
    is the shape every write here takes."""
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path) or ".", exist_ok=True)
    tmp = f"{path}.{os.getpid()}.tmp"
    try:
        os.unlink(tmp)
    except OSError:
        pass
    fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, mode)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "wb" if isinstance(data, (bytes, bytearray)) else "w") as f:
            f.write(data)
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    except BaseException:
        try:
            os.unlink(tmp)
        except OSError:
            pass
        raise


def append_new(path, text, mode=0o644):
    """The same promise for a file that is APPENDED to rather than replaced — the ledger, and the suites' notify
    log. O_NOFOLLOW on the path itself: a link there is a refusal, never a write somewhere else."""
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path) or ".", exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_APPEND | os.O_NOFOLLOW, mode)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "a") as f:
        f.write(text)


def clean(s):
    """What the box says out loud, out of text somebody else wrote. A declaration is a sentence from a commit
    message: it is repeated in the owner's channel, so it may not carry a mention that pings a room, a link
    somebody follows, or markup that makes it look like the box's own words. One line, plain, capped."""
    s = re.sub(r"<[^>]*>", " ", str(s))                        # Slack's own <@U…>, <!channel>, <http…|text>
    s = re.sub(r"(?:https?|mailto|file|ftp)://\S+|www\.\S+", "[link]", s, flags=re.I)
    s = re.sub(r"[@#]([A-Za-z0-9._-])", r"\1", s)              # @here, @channel, @someone, #a-channel
    s = re.sub(r"[`*_~|>]", "", s)                             # mrkdwn emphasis, code, quoting
    return " ".join(s.split())[:MSG_CAP]


def resolve(name):
    """A repo NAME lives under ~/dev; anything with a slash in it is the checkout itself, which is how cc-publish
    names the tree it just published. Either way the channel is the directory's own name."""
    root = name if "/" in name else f"{HOME}/dev/{name}"
    root = os.path.realpath(root)
    return root, os.path.basename(root)


def head_of(root):
    """The default branch as this checkout last saw it. NEVER a fetch of our own: a fetch writes FETCH_HEAD and
    the very ref a landing in the same checkout is pulling, and this runs beside one (cc-publish fetches under
    cc-land's lock; we read what it left)."""
    rc, o = sh(["git", "-C", root, "symbolic-ref", "--quiet", "--short", "refs/remotes/origin/HEAD"])
    br = o.strip().split("/")[-1] if rc == 0 and o.strip() else "main"
    rc, o = sh(["git", "-C", root, "rev-parse", f"refs/remotes/origin/{br}"])
    if rc != 0:
        raise Stop(f"no refs/remotes/origin/{br} in {root} — nothing to follow")
    return o.strip()


def known(root, sha):
    return sh(["git", "-C", root, "cat-file", "-e", f"{sha}^{{commit}}"])[0] == 0


def state_paths(repo):
    if not REPO_RE.match(repo):
        raise Stop(f"'{repo}' is not a name a state file can be keyed by")
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    return f"{STATE}/{repo}.cursor", f"{STATE}/{repo}.posted", f"{STATE}/{repo}.lock"


def read_cursor(path):
    try:
        return open(path).read().strip()
    except OSError:
        return ""


def sent_shas(path):
    """The SHAs this file has already answered for. A line whose outcome is `failed` is one the upload came back
    and SAID it had not sent, so that commit is still owed; anything else — sent, or an intent whose outcome was
    never written because the process died — is done, and is never sent again."""
    state = {}
    try:
        for ln in open(path):
            try:
                r = json.loads(ln)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if r.get("sha"):
                state[r["sha"]] = r.get("to")
    except OSError:
        pass
    return {s for s, to in state.items() if to != "failed"}


def declared(message):
    """The declaration as the landed commit carries it, or "" — the whole decision, offline, in one line."""
    m = MARK.search(message or "")
    return clean(m.group(1)) if m else ""


def marked(root, ref):
    rc, o = sh(["git", "-C", root, "log", "-1", "--format=%B", ref])
    if rc != 0:
        raise Stop(f"no commit {ref} in {root}: {last(o)}")
    return declared(o)


def source_at(root, ref):
    """The source AS IT LANDED, out of the ref — not the working copy, which may be behind what was published."""
    for rel in SRC_RELS:
        rc, o = sh(["git", "-C", root, "show", f"{ref}:{rel}"])
        if rc == 0 and o.strip():
            return rel, o
    raise Stop(f"no overview source at {ref[:8]} (looked for {', '.join(SRC_RELS)})")


def unembedded(table):
    """`pdffonts` output -> why it is not sendable, or "". Its columns are fixed-width and a name can be long
    enough to be one of them, so the `emb` answer is read at the offset the HEADER gives it and any row that does
    not answer yes or no there is a failure, not a pass: the whole point is that nothing unchecked reaches a
    phone, and a font the reader's device has to guess at is exactly what a phone gets wrong."""
    lines = [ln for ln in table.splitlines() if ln.strip()]
    if len(lines) < 3 or "emb" not in lines[0]:
        return "it uses no fonts at all — nothing was rendered"
    col = lines[0].index("emb")
    bad = [ln[:col].strip() or "?" for ln in lines[2:] if ln[col:col + 3].strip() != "yes"]
    return f"these fonts are not embedded in it: {', '.join(bad[:5])}" if bad else ""


def verify(pdf):
    """Two questions, both about the file that would be sent: does it have pages, and are its fonts IN it."""
    rc, o = sh(["pdfinfo", pdf], timeout=60)
    if rc != 0:
        return f"pdfinfo could not read it: {last(o)}"
    m = re.search(r"^Pages:\s+(\d+)", o, re.M)
    if not m or int(m.group(1)) < 1:
        return "it has no pages"
    rc, o = sh(["pdffonts", pdf], timeout=60)
    return f"pdffonts could not read it: {last(o)}" if rc != 0 else unembedded(o)


def build(root, ref):
    """Build it, check it, and put the dated PDF where it can be sent from. Not in the repo: the document is the
    source, and a dated file in git is the very drift this exists to end."""
    rel, tex = source_at(root, ref)
    base = os.path.basename(rel)[:-4] if rel.endswith(".tex") else os.path.basename(rel)
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="cc-arch.") as d:
        write_new(f"{d}/{base}.tex", tex)
        for _ in range(2):   # twice: TikZ places nodes from the previous pass's positions
            # `openin_any=p openout_any=p` is the half `-no-shell-escape` does not cover: paranoid mode refuses
            # TeX's own file reads and writes outside the build directory, so a landed `\input{/…}` of one of
            # this box's files is a build failure and never a paragraph in a document about to be uploaded.
            rc, o = sh(["pdflatex", "-interaction=nonstopmode", "-halt-on-error", "-no-shell-escape",
                        f"{base}.tex"], cwd=d, timeout=TEX_TIMEOUT,
                       env={"openin_any": "p", "openout_any": "p"})
            if rc != 0:
                raise Stop(f"pdflatex failed on {rel} at {ref[:8]}: {last(o, 300)}")
        pdf = f"{d}/{base}.pdf"
        if not os.path.exists(pdf):
            raise Stop(f"pdflatex left no PDF for {rel} at {ref[:8]}")
        why = verify(pdf)
        if why:
            raise Stop(f"the PDF built from {rel} at {ref[:8]} was not sent — {why}")
        out = f"{STATE}/{base}-{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}.pdf"   # the owner's own clock, like every stamp he reads
        write_new(out, open(pdf, "rb").read())
        return out


def post(repo, pdf, text):
    """Into the project's own channel, as a FILE: a link to a path on this box is not something a phone opens.
    CC_NOTIFY_LOG_ONLY is the suites' switch and is honoured here as well as in cc-notify — a test that reached
    this far must still not put a document in a real channel."""
    if os.environ.get("CC_NOTIFY_LOG_ONLY"):
        log = os.environ.get("CC_NOTIFY_LOG") or f"{HOME}/.cc/notify.log"
        append_new(log, f"{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime())}\tarch\t#{repo}\t{pdf}\t{text}\n")
        return "log-only"
    rc, o = sh([f"{BIN}/cc-slack", "post", "--file", pdf, "--to", f"#{repo}",
                "--title", os.path.basename(pdf), "-m", text], timeout=POST_TIMEOUT)
    if rc != 0:
        raise Stop(f"the overview did not reach #{repo}: {last(o)}")
    return "sent"


def message(marks):
    """Plain, one sentence, and the declarations themselves — sanitized where they were read."""
    return f"The architecture changed, so here is the overview again — {'; '.join(w for _, _, w in marks)}"[:1200]


def ledger_write(path, repo, marks, to, pdf):
    at = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())
    append_new(path, "".join(json.dumps({"at": at, "repo": repo, "sha": sha, "pr": pr, "why": why,
                                         "pdf": pdf, "to": to}) + "\n" for sha, pr, why in marks))


def landed(name):
    root, repo = resolve(name)
    if sh(["git", "-C", root, "rev-parse", "--git-dir"])[0] != 0:
        print(f"cc-arch: {root} is not a checkout — nothing to follow")
        return 0
    cursor, ledger, lock = state_paths(repo)
    # ONE TURN PER REPO AT A TIME. The cursor and the ledger are read, then written across a build and an upload
    # that take tens of seconds; two turns overlapping there would each read "not sent yet" and the owner would
    # get the same document twice. Non-blocking on purpose: a second turn has nothing to add and the timer brings
    # the next one along anyway, so it says so and leaves.
    lk = os.fdopen(os.open(lock, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o644), "w")
    try:
        fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError:
        print(f"cc-arch: another turn is working on {repo} — this one has nothing to add")
        return 0
    head = head_of(root)
    cur = read_cursor(cursor)
    if not cur or not known(root, cur):
        write_new(cursor, head + "\n")
        print(f"cc-arch: following {repo} from {head[:8]} — nothing posted for what landed before this")
        return 0
    if cur == head:
        return 0
    rc, o = sh(["git", "-C", root, "log", "--reverse", f"--format={REC}%H{FLD}%s{FLD}%B", f"{cur}..{head}"])
    if rc != 0:
        raise Stop(f"cannot list what landed in {repo}: {last(o)}")
    sent, marks = sent_shas(ledger), []
    for rec in o.split(REC):
        if not rec.strip():
            continue
        sha, subj, body = (rec.split(FLD, 2) + ["", ""])[:3]
        sha = sha.strip()
        if not sha or sha in sent:
            continue
        why = declared(body)
        if why:
            m = PRNUM.search(subj)
            marks.append((sha, m.group(1) if m else "", why))
    if marks:
        pdf = build(root, head)
        # POST ONCE. The intent goes down BEFORE the upload: a kill between the two leaves a record saying this
        # document was already owed to the channel, and the next turn reads those SHAs as answered for. Only an
        # upload that came back and SAID it failed is written as failed, and only that is tried again.
        ledger_write(ledger, repo, marks, "sending", pdf)
        try:
            where = post(repo, pdf, message(marks))
        except Stop:
            ledger_write(ledger, repo, marks, "failed", pdf)
            raise
        ledger_write(ledger, repo, marks, where, pdf)
        print(f"cc-arch: {os.path.basename(pdf)} {where} to #{repo}"
              + ("".join(f" (PR #{pr})" for _, pr, _ in marks if pr)))
    write_new(cursor, head + "\n")
    return 0


def main(argv):
    if not argv or argv[0] in ("-h", "--help"):
        print(__doc__.strip())
        return 0
    cmd, rest = argv[0], argv[1:]
    if cmd == "selfcheck":
        return selfcheck()
    try:
        if cmd == "landed" and len(rest) == 1:
            return landed(rest[0])
        if cmd == "build" and len(rest) in (1, 2):
            root, _ = resolve(rest[0])
            print(build(root, rest[1] if len(rest) > 1 else head_of(root)))
            return 0
        if cmd == "marked" and len(rest) == 2:
            root, _ = resolve(rest[0])
            why = marked(root, rest[1])
            if why:
                print(why)
            return 0 if why else 1
    except Stop as e:
        # A turn this file could not finish is never a caller's failure: cc-publish has already pushed, and the
        # next turn asks again from a cursor that did not move.
        print(f"cc-arch: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 0 if cmd == "landed" else 1
    print("usage: cc-arch landed <repo> | build <repo> [<ref>] | marked <repo> <ref> | selfcheck", file=sys.stderr)
    return 2


# ── selfcheck ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FIXTURES ONLY: a HOME of its own with its own repos and remotes under it, and a stub `cc-slack` that records
# its argv instead of uploading anything. No repository of this box's is read, nothing leaves the machine, and no
# state outside the temp HOME is written. The ONE thing it reads from this tree is the overview source next to
# this file — the document is the deliverable, so a source that stopped building is this tool's failure and not
# somebody's later surprise. Every case that builds is SKIPPED, not failed, where pdflatex is not installed.
SLACK_STUB = """#!/usr/bin/env bash
printf 'cc-slack %s\\n' "$*" >> "$CC_SC_REC"
[ -z "${CC_SC_SLACK_HANG:-}" ] || sleep 60
[ -z "${CC_SC_SLACK_DOWN:-}" ] || { echo "channel not found" >&2; exit 1; }
"""
# A one-page document in the same dialect the real one is written in — plain pdflatex, psnfss (charter), nothing
# outside texlive-latex-recommended — so the cases build in a fraction of a second and still exercise the real
# pdflatex, pdfinfo and pdffonts. The real source gets its own case below.
TINY = ("\\documentclass[10pt,a4paper]{article}\n\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n\\usepackage{charter}\n"
        "\\pagestyle{empty}\n\\begin{document}\nThe shape of it.\n\\end{document}\n")


def selfcheck():
    n = f = 0

    def ok(what, cond):
        nonlocal n, f
        print(("  ok   " if cond else "  FAIL ") + what)
        n += 1
        f += int(not cond)

    th = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-arch-sc.")
    try:
        # ── what needs no build, and so runs everywhere ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
        ok("the declaration is a line in the first column of a commit BODY: the word inside a sentence is prose, "
           "an indented quotation of the instruction is prose, a squashed commit's SUBJECT is prose because the "
           "squash bullets it — which is why the docs say body, never subject — and a line of its own is read "
           "back without its whitespace",
           declared("This is not an ARCHITECTURE: change, it only mentions it.") == ""
           and declared("  ARCHITECTURE: quoted in a paragraph about this file") == ""
           and declared("a squash subject (#9)\n\n* ARCHITECTURE: on a bulleted subject line") == ""
           and declared("a subject\n\nARCHITECTURE:   the box grew a steward  \n\nmore prose") == "the box grew a steward")
        said_out = clean("ARCHITECTURE <!channel> <@U123> see *this* `now` at https://evil.example/x @here #general "
                         + "y" * 400)
        ok("what the box repeats is sanitized where it is read: no mention that pings a room, no link somebody "
           "follows, no markup that makes it look like the box's own words, one line, capped",
           "<" not in said_out and "@" not in said_out and "`" not in said_out and "*" not in said_out
           and "evil.example" not in said_out and "[link]" in said_out and "\n" not in said_out
           and len(said_out) <= MSG_CAP)
        hdr = ("name                                 type              encoding         emb sub uni object ID\n"
               "------------------------------------ ----------------- ---------------- --- --- --- ---------\n")
        ok("the font check refuses a document with no fonts at all and one whose fonts the reader's device would "
           "have to supply, and passes one that carries its own",
           unembedded("") != ""
           and "Helvetica" in unembedded(hdr + "Helvetica                            Type 1            WinAnsi          no  no  no       7  0\n")
           and unembedded(hdr + "ABCDEF+CharterBT-Roman               Type 1            Custom           yes yes yes      9  0\n") == "")
        # THE WRITE HELPERS, on links planted where each of them writes.
        os.makedirs(f"{th}/w", exist_ok=True)
        open(f"{th}/w/victim", "w").write("untouched\n")
        os.symlink(f"{th}/w/victim", f"{th}/w/pdf")
        os.symlink(f"{th}/w/victim", f"{th}/w/led")
        write_new(f"{th}/w/pdf", "the real thing\n")
        try:
            append_new(f"{th}/w/led", "a line\n")
            appended = False
        except OSError:
            appended = True
        ok("a link planted where this writes is replaced, never written through — the file it pointed at is "
           "untouched, and an APPEND onto one is refused outright",
           open(f"{th}/w/victim").read() == "untouched\n" and not os.path.islink(f"{th}/w/pdf")
           and open(f"{th}/w/pdf").read() == "the real thing\n" and appended and os.path.islink(f"{th}/w/led"))

        if not shutil.which("pdflatex"):
            print("  ·    pdflatex is not installed here, so every case that builds a document is skipped "
                  "(install texlive-latex-recommended and texlive-pictures to run them)")
            print(f"cc-arch selfcheck: {n - f} passed, {f} failed")
            return 1 if f else 0

        # ── the fixture box ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        env0 = dict(os.environ)
        sbin, rec = f"{th}/bin", f"{th}/rec"
        for d in (sbin, f"{th}/dev"):
            os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
        open(f"{sbin}/cc-slack", "w").write(SLACK_STUB)
        os.chmod(f"{sbin}/cc-slack", 0o755)
        root, origin = f"{th}/dev/myrepo", f"{th}/origin.git"
        git = ["git", "-c", "user.name=t", "-c", "user.email=t@t", "-c", "commit.gpgsign=false"]
        sh(["git", "init", "-q", "--bare", "-b", "main", origin])
        sh(["git", "init", "-q", "-b", "main", root])
        os.makedirs(f"{root}/core/docs", exist_ok=True)
        open(f"{root}/core/docs/autobox-overview.tex", "w").write(TINY)

        def commit(msg, touch=None):
            if touch:
                open(f"{root}/{touch}", "a").write("x\n")
            sh(git + ["-C", root, "add", "-A"])
            sh(git + ["-C", root, "commit", "-q", "--allow-empty", "-m", msg])
            sh(git + ["-C", root, "push", "-q", origin, "main"])
            sh(git + ["-C", root, "fetch", "-q", origin, "+main:refs/remotes/origin/main"])
            return sh(["git", "-C", root, "rev-parse", "HEAD"])[1].strip()

        sh(git + ["-C", root, "remote", "add", "origin", origin])
        commit("the first thing")

        def cmdline(*argv, **envx):
            env = dict(env0, HOME=th, CC_ARCH_BIN=sbin, PATH=f"{sbin}:{env0.get('PATH', '')}", CC_SC_REC=rec)
            for k in ("CC_NOTIFY_LOG_ONLY", "CC_ARCH_SOURCE", "CC_SC_SLACK_DOWN", "CC_SC_SLACK_HANG"):
                env.pop(k, None)
            env.update({k: v for k, v in envx.items() if v is not None})
            return [sys.executable, os.path.realpath(__file__)] + list(argv), env

        def run(*argv, **envx):
            a, env = cmdline(*argv, **envx)
            return subprocess.run(a, capture_output=True, text=True, env=env, timeout=300)

        def said():
            try:
                return open(rec).read()
            except OSError:
                return ""

        def cursor():
            return read_cursor(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.cursor")

        def pdfs():
            d = f"{th}/.cc/state/arch"
            return sorted(x for x in os.listdir(d) if x.endswith(".pdf")) if os.path.isdir(d) else []

        # THE FIRST TURN NEVER ANSWERS FOR THE PAST.
        head = sh(["git", "-C", root, "rev-parse", "refs/remotes/origin/main"])[1].strip()
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        ok("a first turn writes the cursor where the repo is and posts nothing — it never answers for the "
           "history that landed before it existed",
           r.returncode == 0 and cursor() == head and said() == "" and pdfs() == [])

        # A LANDING THAT DECLARES NOTHING — and it is the one that rewrote the source, so a diff would have said yes.
        sha = commit("the source, rewritten, saying nothing about it (#11)\n\nReflowed the overview. Nothing "
                     "about the shape of the box changed.", touch="core/docs/autobox-overview.tex")
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        ok("a landing that declares nothing posts NOTHING — not even the one that rewrote the overview itself, "
           "because what counts is declared and never read out of a diff",
           r.returncode == 0 and "cc-slack" not in said() and pdfs() == [] and cursor() == sha)

        # …AND ONE THAT DOES, read out of the commit that landed and nowhere else.
        sha = commit("the steward takes the routine events (#12)\n\n* some prose first\n\n"
                     "ARCHITECTURE: routine events go to a steward now\n\nmore prose")
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        up = [ln for ln in said().splitlines() if ln.startswith("cc-slack")]
        built = pdfs()
        ok("a landing that declares itself an architecture revision rebuilds the overview and puts the FILE in "
           "the project's channel, once, saying what changed in the words the change used",
           r.returncode == 0 and len(up) == 1 and "--file" in up[0] and "--to #myrepo" in up[0]
           and "routine events go to a steward now" in up[0] and len(built) == 1 and cursor() == sha)
        ok("…and what was sent is a real PDF with its fonts inside it — the check that runs before anything is sent",
           bool(built) and verify(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/{built[0]}") == "")

        # THE LEDGER IS KEYED ON THE COMMIT, so winding the cursor back sends nothing.
        write_new(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.cursor", head + "\n")
        write_new(rec, "")
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        ok("a cursor wound all the way back re-reads the same revision and sends nothing: what the ledger keys "
           "on is the commit that landed, which a rewind cannot change",
           r.returncode == 0 and "cc-slack" not in said() and cursor() == sha
           and f'"sha": "{sha}"' in open(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.posted").read())

        # AN UPLOAD THAT COMES BACK FAILED IS STILL OWED; ONE THAT WAS NEVER ANSWERED IS NOT.
        before = cursor()
        commit("a second shape change (#13)\n\nARCHITECTURE: a second shape change")
        write_new(rec, "")
        r = run("landed", "myrepo", CC_SC_SLACK_DOWN="1")
        ok("an upload that comes back saying it failed leaves the cursor where it was and is written down as "
           "failed, so the revision is not silently lost",
           r.returncode == 0 and cursor() == before
           and '"to": "failed"' in open(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.posted").read())
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        ok("…and the next turn sends it", r.returncode == 0 and "--file" in said() and cursor() != before)

        # A KILL BETWEEN THE INTENT AND THE UPLOAD SENDS ONCE, NOT TWICE.
        before = cursor()
        commit("a third shape change (#14)\n\nARCHITECTURE: a third shape change")
        write_new(rec, "")
        a, env = cmdline("landed", "myrepo", CC_SC_SLACK_HANG="1")
        p = subprocess.Popen(a, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, env=env)
        end = time.time() + 60
        while time.time() < end and "cc-slack" not in said():
            time.sleep(0.1)
        hung = "cc-slack" in said()
        p.kill()
        p.wait(timeout=30)
        write_new(rec, "")
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        ok("a turn killed between writing down what it was about to send and the upload answering does NOT send "
           "the same document again on the next turn — the intent is the record, not the answer",
           hung and r.returncode == 0 and "cc-slack" not in said()
           and '"to": "sending"' in open(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.posted").read())

        # TWO TURNS AT ONCE ARE ONE TURN.
        write_new(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.cursor", before + "\n")
        write_new(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.posted", "")
        write_new(rec, "")
        held = open(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.lock", "w")
        fcntl.flock(held, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        quiet = r.returncode == 0 and "cc-slack" not in said() and cursor() == before
        held.close()
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        ok("a turn that finds another already working on the repo adds nothing and leaves, and the one after it "
           "sends — the cursor and the ledger are read and written across a build and an upload, and the owner "
           "must not be handed the same document twice",
           quiet and r.returncode == 0 and "--file" in said() and cursor() != before)

        # THE SUITES' OWN SWITCH, HONOURED HERE TOO.
        write_new(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.cursor", before + "\n")
        write_new(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.posted", "")
        write_new(rec, "")
        r = run("landed", "myrepo", CC_NOTIFY_LOG_ONLY="1", CC_NOTIFY_LOG=f"{th}/notify.log")
        ok("under CC_NOTIFY_LOG_ONLY the document is built and written down and cc-slack is never called at all, "
           "so a suite that reaches this far still cannot put a file in a real channel",
           r.returncode == 0 and "cc-slack" not in said()
           and "#myrepo" in open(f"{th}/notify.log").read())

        # A SOURCE THAT WILL NOT BUILD, AND ONE THAT TRIES TO READ THE BOX ON ITS WAY.
        before = cursor()
        write_new(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.posted", "")
        write_new(rec, "")
        open(f"{root}/core/docs/autobox-overview.tex", "w").write(
            "\\documentclass{article}\n\\begin{document}\n\\undefinedcontrolsequencexyz\n\\end{document}\n")
        commit("the overview no longer builds (#15)\n\nARCHITECTURE: y")
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        ok("a source that does not build sends nothing and moves nothing — the owner is never handed a document "
           "this file could not make",
           r.returncode == 0 and "cc-slack" not in said() and cursor() == before)
        secret = f"{th}/secret.tex"
        open(secret, "w").write("CANARYFROMOUTSIDETHEBUILD\n")
        open(f"{root}/core/docs/autobox-overview.tex", "w").write(
            TINY.replace("The shape of it.", "The shape of it. \\input{" + secret + "}"))
        commit("the overview reads a file of the box's (#16)\n\nARCHITECTURE: z")
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        leaked = ""
        for x in pdfs():
            leaked += sh(["pdftotext", f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/{x}", "-"], timeout=60)[1]
        ok("a landed source that reads a file from outside the build directory does not build, so nothing of "
           "this box's can be carried into a document that is about to be uploaded",
           r.returncode == 0 and "cc-slack" not in said() and cursor() == before
           and "CANARYFROMOUTSIDETHEBUILD" not in leaked)
        open(f"{root}/core/docs/autobox-overview.tex", "w").write(TINY)
        commit("the overview builds again (#17)\n\nnothing declared here")
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        ok("…and once it builds, the revisions that were waiting go out together, in ONE message and one file",
           r.returncode == 0 and len([ln for ln in said().splitlines() if ln.startswith("cc-slack")]) == 1
           and "y; z" in said() and cursor() == sh(["git", "-C", root, "rev-parse", "HEAD"])[1].strip())

        # A LINK PLANTED WHERE THE DOCUMENT GOES.
        write_new(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.cursor", before + "\n")
        write_new(f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/myrepo.posted", "")
        write_new(rec, "")
        open(f"{th}/outside", "w").write("untouched\n")
        target = f"{th}/.cc/state/arch/autobox-overview-{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}.pdf"
        os.path.exists(target) and os.remove(target)
        os.symlink(f"{th}/outside", target)
        r = run("landed", "myrepo")
        ok("a link planted at the path the document is written to is replaced, not followed — the file it named "
           "is untouched and the document still goes out",
           r.returncode == 0 and open(f"{th}/outside").read() == "untouched\n"
           and not os.path.islink(target) and "--file" in said())

        # THE REAL DOCUMENT. Its source is the deliverable, so a source that stopped building fails HERE and not
        # on the morning the box has something to say. Built through the tool's own door in the fixture HOME —
        # nothing of this box's state is written, and the copy under test is the one committed in this tree.
        real = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(BIN), "docs/autobox-overview.tex")
        if os.path.exists(real):
            sh(git + ["-C", root, "checkout", "-q", "-B", "real"])
            open(f"{root}/core/docs/autobox-overview.tex", "w").write(open(real).read())
            sh(git + ["-C", root, "add", "-A"])
            sh(git + ["-C", root, "commit", "-q", "-m", "the real overview"])
            ref = sh(["git", "-C", root, "rev-parse", "HEAD"])[1].strip()
            r = run("build", root, ref)
            out = r.stdout.strip()
            ok("THE OVERVIEW ITSELF builds with plain pdflatex and psnfss fonts, in paranoid file mode, and "
               "passes the check that gates the send — the document is what this tool exists to deliver"
               + (f" ({last(r.stderr, 160)})" if r.returncode else ""),
               r.returncode == 0 and out.endswith(".pdf") and os.path.exists(out) and verify(out) == "")
        else:
            ok("the overview source sits next to this file, so its build is checked here", False)
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(th, ignore_errors=True)
    print(f"cc-arch selfcheck: {n - f} passed, {f} failed")
    return 1 if f else 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
